  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9639d95d5d9bebb40baa4bc4d106e699, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 5) Why is the date of an image or an article on a post important when judging
    its accuracy?
  answers:
  - "The date doesn\u2019t matter if the content of the post is still relevant."
  - The date helps determine if the information is current or outdated, and whether
    it may have  been misrepresented as recent news.
  - Older posts are always more accurate because they have been fact-checked over
    time.
  - The date is irrelevant because fake news is always based on recent events.
  correctAnswers: 2
